+# Workflow navigation and evidence boundaries
+
+Source snapshot: `9de08d78db6526e2ce2dd66cedd5e63f600424bd`. This index describes **37 workflow configurations**, not 37 completed checks or accepted mathematical results. The exact triggers, filters, commands, permissions, and pinned inputs remain in each linked YAML file. No workflow was launched to prepare this guide.
+
+## Read a workflow before reading a status badge
+
+Every listed workflow has a path-filtered push trigger at this snapshot. Some additionally declare a pull-request trigger or manual dispatch. The table abbreviates push filters; inspect the YAML for every exact pattern and for any separate pull-request filters. A push trigger restricted to its own YAML is not a continuous check of every change to the associated mathematical source. A branch pattern in a retained workflow does not establish that the branch still exists.
+
+Job names such as `verify`, `kernel-check`, `snapshot`, `publish`, or `runtime` are configuration identifiers, not execution evidence. Distinguish a source export or toolchain bootstrap from a theorem build, a finite-certificate replay, an axiom audit, and independent semantic review. For a result, retain the actual run ID, head commit, attempt, job/step conclusion, complete relevant logs, and the checked source/dependency hashes. A successful unrelated job cannot supply missing verification for another contribution.
+
