+## Side effects and historical-layout assumptions
+
+The [English publication workflow](workflows/agent1-english-publish.yml) has separate candidate preparation and publication jobs. Its source checks a generated bundle and an exact parent before a non-force main update. The [cleanup retirement workflow](workflows/p196-cleanup-retire.yml) concerns branch retirement, not proof verification. Several other workflows declare publication steps or write permissions. Do not edit or dispatch these merely to test a documentation sentence; preserve the integration ownership rules in [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md).
+
+Some retained workflows name pre-reorganization contribution paths. Check the workflow's own source revision and setup steps before declaring such a path missing or substituting a flattened filename. The [research replay guide](../proofs/README.md#verification-using-the-original-layout) explains the separate original-layout wrappers; it does not automatically repair, rerun, or validate every workflow listed here.
+
+An artifact name is not sufficient provenance. Keep its workflow run and source revision with the retained payload and hashes. Temporary artifact transport is not a permanent replacement for the repository's publication records. The [English reading index](../proofs/english/README.md) distinguishes translation views from archived originals; the [research status](../proofs/STATUS.md) retains the mathematical scope boundary.
+
+## Catalogue maintenance
+
+This census used the hash-checked 35-workflow source set from the existing inventory artifact at `e5e381e2800a86bf948bc2ec93dd5e2ba064236e`, a complete commit comparison showing those files unchanged, and direct pinned reads of the two later English workflows. It did not inspect every historical workflow version or certify every shell command. Recount and recheck the YAML after source changes; do not hand-edit a historical build log to match this navigation index.
